#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Forced-command dispatcher for the Luca production profile.

SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND is parsed as data and is never executed.  The production
paths below are intentionally not configurable.  Tests may mirror that fixed
tree beneath a temporary root only when this file is *not* running from its
installed production pathname, two explicit environment gates are present,
and a sentinel file exists.  Thus the seam is unavailable to the installed
forced command and cannot be selected through SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND.

The deploy role exposes only frozen top-level names.  ``deploy backup`` makes
and rotates the recovery point, ``deploy transfer`` starts a fixed rsync
receiver, ``deploy promote <content-hash>`` builds and verifies out of place,
and ``deploy restart`` restarts the two fixed user units.  ``restore`` selects
the newest recovery point and ``accept [deletion]`` runs the fixed real-turn
mode-restoring acceptance (with the optional production render-file subset
gate).  These phases let the MBP orchestrator apply the unconditional restore
rules without widening the SSH command surface.
"""

